{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/931515-could-a-solar-leverage-their-bloodline-for-safety-in-nechara","id":931515,"title":"Could a Solar leverage their bloodline for safety in Nechara?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T12:32:33-07:00","id":931515,"title":"Could a Solar leverage their bloodline for safety in Nechara?","content":"If they are willing to take in the blood of ghosts and <b>literal</b> demons then surely they would be alright with bargaining with an Anathema right? Also it never actually mentions how they feel about taking in Lunars, Liminials (Unsure if they can reproduce) and other Exalts?<br /> Just curious about opinions and theories regarding this, since your average Exalt will probably be far more reasonable with the bargains than various Spirits (given their varying degrees of delusional egomania) and Nechara is explicitly in severe debt. Also I imagine that an Exalts bloodline is probably more potent than your average god-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:05:21-07:00","id":931530,"title":"","content":"Literal demons run the gamut of safety and pleasantry, so the term alone doesn't exactly imply a devil may care attitude.<br /> <br /> I would say the biggest obstacle to adding Celestial Exalted is that it's a lot less reliable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:19:18-07:00","id":931537,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of ways that this could play out, though off hand it seems fairly reasonable even if rather dangerous. I imagine that if it were to come out that someone was Moon-touched or Sun-touched or whatever, there would likely be some kind response, possibly even a Wyld Hunt. <br /> <br /> Basically, if a Sun-touched or Moon-touched had power that made them obviously related to one of the Anathema, and it was suspected or known that the nation had climbed into bed with the Anathema, there would probably be a response from nearby Dragon Blooded. The Anathema are viewed as a nigh-universal threat, and even the Realm might decide to respond. <br /> <br /> So traditionally, I don't think Nechara would have agreed to something like that - the risks of having a Wyld Hunt descend on your nation (or even a full on Realm invasion) would be much too dangerous and outweigh whatever benefits you might get. However, with the defeat of the Tepet Legions and the fact that the Realm is in disarray, suddenly the risks of climbing into bed with the Anathema aren't quite as serious. <br /> <br /> Still, there are probably plenty of stories and fables (&quot;The Foolish King and the Lunar Anathema&quot;) throughout Creation about the dangers of trusting anathema that even many in Nechara might hesitate or reject the idea. <br /> <br /> Ultimately adding a Solar's power to one's family line seems like something that one particular family might choose to do, while trying to keep it secret from everyone else, rather than something like a national policy that the nation would be willing to get behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}